---
// Recent work: what changed, with a door to the page for each thing.
//
// Written 2026-11-24 for the operator after a long session. Not a generated catalogue: a dated
// summary of the session's work, each item linking to the page where it lives. The commits are
// read at request time, so the list cannot go stale.
import { execFileSync } from "node:child_process";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { repoRoot } from "../lib/gallery.js";

const commits = execFileSync("git", ["log", "--oneline", "-28"], { cwd: repoRoot(), encoding: "utf8" })
  .trim().split("\n");

const named = [
  ["c-0420", "semicubical", "Neile's parabola; a cusp at the origin"],
  ["c-0421", "kappa", "Gutschoven's kappa; r = cot θ"],
  ["c-0422", "strophoid", "the right strophoid; the loop closes at the node"],
  ["c-0423", "pear", "x² = y³(1 − y); the cusp at the origin"],
  ["c-0424", "piriform 2×", "the water drop stretched 2× on x"],
  ["c-0425", "bean", "the quartic bean, two branches"],
  ["c-0426", "heart", "the smooth sextic heart, two sampled halves"],
  ["c-0427", "squircle", "Lamé's quartic, |x|⁴ + |y|⁴ = 1"],
  ["c-0428", "rounded square", "four edges and four exact quarter arcs"],
];
---

<BaseLayout title="recent work" pageTitle="Recent work: 23–24 November 2026">
  <style is:global>
    .rw { display: grid; gap: 20px; margin-top: 18px; }
    .rw section { border: 1px solid #e6dccb; background: #fffef9; padding: 14px 16px; }
    .rw h2 { margin: 0 0 6px; }
    .rw p, .rw li { line-height: 1.55; }
    .rw .when { font: 12px/1.4 ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; color: #8a7a62; }
    .rw .cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(15rem, 1fr)); gap: 10px; margin-top: 10px; }
    .rw figure { margin: 0; border: 1px solid #eee3d3; background: #fff; padding: 6px; }
    .rw figure img { display: block; width: 100%; height: 130px; object-fit: contain; background: #fff; }
    .rw figcaption { font: 12px/1.4 ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; color: #5a4a36; margin-top: 4px; }
    .rw code { font-size: 0.92em; }
    .rw .commits { columns: 2; font: 12px/1.5 ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; color: #5a4a36; }
    @media (max-width: 800px) { .rw .commits { columns: 1; } }
  </style>

  <h1>Recent work — 23–24 November 2026</h1>
  <p class="lead">What was built and what was proved, newest first, with the page for each.
    Every claim here is one a check or a printed number already backs.</p>

  <div class="rw">
    <section>
      <h2>The trim desk — cut a curve's legs off at rational t</h2>
      <p class="when">2026-11-24 · <a href="/trim/">/trim/</a> · <a href="/plates">/plates</a></p>
      <p>Type two fractions, <code>p/q</code> and <code>r/s</code>: t = 0 is the first station,
        t = 1 the last. The stations between the cuts are kept and the legs dropped; the cut
        points sit exactly on the fractions. A decimal is refused on purpose.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The list leads with the <b>196 curves on the plates</b> in their star order; the
          209 other cuttable records follow. Every plate card carries a <b>trim</b> link.</li>
        <li>A curve stored as speed rows is <b>sampled</b> with the plate's own sampler (700
          stations) and the saved record says so; a four-branch curve is cut per branch and
          every branch's two cut points are marked.</li>
        <li>Saves beside the parent with the four side values; proved by clicking on
          <code>c-0274</code> (1/5 → 4/5: 113 kept, 76 dropped).</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="cards">
        <figure><img src="/figures/c-0274.png" alt="double-1-se-1, the trim example" />
          <figcaption><a href="/trim/c-0274">c-0274</a> · cut its legs</figcaption></figure>
        <figure><img src="/figures/c-0416.png" alt="the cruciform, four branches" />
          <figcaption><a href="/trim/c-0416">c-0416</a> · four branches</figcaption></figure>
        <figure><img src="/figures/c-0001.png" alt="amper, a rows record" />
          <figcaption><a href="/trim/c-0001">c-0001</a> · sampled from rows</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The cut desk answers, and the preview no longer saves</h2>
      <p class="when">2026-11-23 · <a href="/cut/">/cut/</a> · <a href="/cut/c-0274">/cut/c-0274</a></p>
      <ul>
        <li>The save used to wait for the plate and figure renders inside the request (up to
          180 s), so the button read "cutting…" while the record was already written. It now
          returns at once; the renders run in a detached child under a lock.</li>
        <li>A dot cut previews the kept arc, never the line's halves.</li>
        <li>Both desks' <b>preview buttons were saving</b> (the handler checked an id that a
          button without one does not have). Fixed on both, with a browser check.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Every named classical curve is now a record</h2>
      <p class="when">2026-11-23/24 · <a href="/extra-curves/">/extra-curves/</a> ·
        <a href="/figures/">/figures/</a></p>
      <p>Nine added, sampled from the generators' own equations, each with a plate and a
        figure. The missing list is <b>0 of 29</b>; the "quartic" and "sextic" it used to
        propose were speed examples, never named curves.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        {named.map(([uid, name, why]) => (
          <figure>
            <img src={`/figures/${uid}.png`} alt={name} loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption><a href={`/tune/${uid}`}>{uid}</a> {name}<br />{why}</figcaption>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The root lab has both missing axes</h2>
      <p class="when">2026-11-24 · <a href="/roots/">/roots/</a></p>
      <p>A second mirrored root pair (<code>p₂/q₂</code>) and a variable x row{" "}
        <code>A + B(t² − t)</code>. The maths test pins the curve's mirror about its vertical
        centre; a browser check moves both controls and requires the facts line to follow.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>A coupler curve with two nodes, and the bug that hid them</h2>
      <p class="when">2026-11-24 · <a href="/sandbox/">/sandbox/</a> ·
        <a href="/tune/c-0429">c-0429</a></p>
      <p>The coupler search kept only "4+ crossing pairs" — impossible, since a four-bar
        coupler curve has at most <b>three</b> double points. With the threshold at 2 and a
        Grashof filter, 8,000 Grashof linkages give <b>nine</b> curves with two double points
        and none with three. The most symmetric is a candidate record:
        crank 1.364 · coupler 4.102 · rocker 4.007 · ground 1.652 · point (2.322, 0.376),
        mirror gap 1.7 %.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        <figure><img src="/figures/c-0429.png" alt="the two-node coupler curve" />
          <figcaption><a href="/tune/c-0429">c-0429</a> coupler-two-node · 721 sampled stations</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The book set is whole and checked</h2>
      <p class="when">2026-11-23 · <a href="/book">/book</a> · <a href="/plates">/plates</a></p>
      <p>Twenty-two curves had no plate; rendered. <code>check_book_plates.mjs</code> reads
        every PNG header: <b>406 plates, 3000 px on the long side, 300 dpi</b>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The records have a status and a PNG flag</h2>
      <p class="when">2026-11-23 · <a href="/extra-curves/">/extra-curves/</a> ·
        <a href="/class-v/">/class-v/</a></p>
      <p>Every curve carries <code>status</code> (kept, in-progress, temporary, proposed) and
        <code>pngIgnored</code>; page-only curves are <code>Study</code> rows. Git follows the
        flag: 764 tracked renders were untracked, files kept on disk;
        <code>set_png_flag.mjs &lt;uid&gt; keep|ignore</code> flips one.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The working rules that changed</h2>
      <p class="when">2026-11-24 · <code>AGENTS.md</code> · <code>state/PORT-int.md</code></p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>New code is TypeScript</b>, and any <code>.js</code> being changed is converted in
          the same commit; DeepSeek2 owns moving what already exists. The app is under
          <code>astro/tsconfigs/strict</code>, every <code>src/**/*.ts</code> is checked, and
          <code>prebuild</code> runs <code>astro check</code>.</li>
        <li><b>The operator's asks are a register</b> (<code>state/ASKS-int.md</code>), checked by
          <code>scripts/check_asks.py</code>; a repeated ask is a fault, not a nudge.</li>
        <li><b>Two said rolls</b>: the main chat's and the sidechat's own, each checked for a row
          per statement and proof on every done row.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The last commits</h2>
      <p class="when">read from git at request time</p>
      <ol class="commits">
        {commits.map((line) => <li>{line}</li>)}
      </ol>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
